.KEY x
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; FAT versus SFS on the same card, same driver (sdcard.md, the 2x2 matrix).
;
; The Pi boots from FAT and always will, so SYS: does not move. The second
; partition -- MBR type 0x2f, which partition.library maps to DOSType SFS\0 --
; is a work volume beside it. Everything below the filesystem is identical.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[sfs] devices the system knows:"
Info >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[sfs] assigns and volumes:"
Assign >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[sfs] done listing"
